", "Role, context and instructions", "Professional prompting techniques", "Templates for office tasks", "Improving AI responses"]}, {"name": "AI for Email & Business Communication", "description": "Professional communication with AI", "chapters": ["Professional email writing", "Email replies and follow-ups", "Business proposals and letters", "Meeting communication", "Tone, grammar and proofreading"]}, {"name": "AI for Excel, Sheets, Data & Reports", "description": "Work with spreadsheets and business data", "chapters": ["Excel formula assistance", "Data cleaning concepts", "Tables and reports", "Data analysis with AI", "Business insights and summaries"]}, {"name": "Final Practical Project & Certification", "description": "Complete office automation project", "chapters": ["Word Professional Document", "Resume Preparation", "Official Letter", "Excel Data Entry Project", "Excel MIS Report", "Excel Dashboard", "PowerPoint Presentation", "Professional Email Task", "Access Database Project", "Office Documentation", "PDF Management Task", "Practical Examination", "Viva / Interview", "Final Skill Assessment", "Course Certification"]}]}$J$::jsonb as j),
courses as (
  select c."id", c."code", e.value as mods
    from data, jsonb_each(data.j) e
    join public.courses c on upper(c."code") = e.key and c."deletedAt" is null
   where not exists (select 1 from public.course_modules m where m."courseId" = c."id" and m."deletedAt" is null)
),
mods as (
  insert into public.course_modules ("courseId", name, description, "sortOrder")
  select co."id", m.value->>'name', nullif(m.value->>'description',''), m.ordinality
    from courses co, jsonb_array_elements(co.mods) with ordinality m
  returning id, "courseId", "sortOrder"
),
chs as (
  insert into public.course_chapters ("moduleId", "courseId", name, "sortOrder")
  select mo.id, mo."courseId", ch.value #>> '{}', ch.ordinality
    from mods mo
    join courses co on co."id" = mo."courseId"
    cross join lateral jsonb_array_elements(co.mods -> (mo."sortOrder"::int - 1) -> 'chapters') with ordinality ch
  returning 1
)
select (select count(*) from mods) as modules_added, (select count(*) from chs) as chapters_added;
